## 9. Conclusion

Do not try to control every future action of an AGI. Control the dynamical conditions that determine which stable behavioral regimes remain reachable.

The mathematical foundation is:

\[
\boxed{
\text{Existence}
\;\rightarrow\;
\text{Viable Accessibility}
\;\rightarrow\;
\text{Reachability}
\;\rightarrow\;
\text{Invariance/Stability}
}
\]

A safe equilibrium that exists but is not viably reachable is mathematically real but operationally inert. 
The problem is not to find the equilibrium; it is to **construct and maintain the corridor** through which it can be accessed. 
Viability theory, reachability analysis, and control barrier functions provide the machinery to answer this question rigorously 
and to design interventions that preserve access when it is threatened.
